  "note": "A world_buildings fragment (src/buildings.cpp): the system JSON names it under \"world_buildings_files\" and the loader merges these entries into its own \"world_buildings\". lat_deg/lon_deg are DEGREES, lon east-positive (west longitudes negative); equirect.h maps them onto the body's rotating frame and the heightmap is geographic, so these are the sites' real coordinates -- the launch centre's own position, not the nearest town's. They are given to 4 dp, far finer than res/heightmaps/earth/earth_hm.i16 samples (0.133 deg, ~14.8 km): a site smaller than one map pixel (an island, a barrier beach) reads as sea level there, and with \"ocean\": \"flat\" its pad deck lands at sea level rather than at its true elevation. height_m lifts the deck above the ground sampled at the site's own dir; space_port.obj's 10 m of slab carries it down through the relief across the rest of the footprint (tests/test_buildings.cpp pins both). The FIRST entry is the game's default site: find_launch_site falls back to the first VAB_LAUNCH_PAD, and merged fragments come before a system's inline world_buildings.",
